# Keys allowed to sign a gate receipt (scripts/gate-receipt.sh verify).
#
# CI reuses the gate a developer ran locally when that run is published as a
# signed tag under refs/gate/<head-sha>, and this file is the trust anchor for
# that signature: an SSH signature is only evidence if the key is one this
# repository decided to trust. One signer per line, in ssh-keygen
# allowed_signers format:
#
#   <principal> [options] <keytype> <key>
#
# The principal is the key's comment — the identity git reports when it verifies
# the signature — and it must match what the signing key carries. Rotating the
# signing key means adding the new line here; until it is added, CI falls back to
# running the whole gate, which is the safe direction.
